            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0543" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34582/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Walton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-07-03T16:00:00-00:44">July 3, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 4—2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Department’s number 40, June 30, 9 p.m. President Barclay is generally
                    agreeable to the suggestion and feels it is now necessary to meet with trust
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">trusted?</hi>] advisers before giving a definitive
                    reply which will be forthcoming within the next 2 days. I am confident it will
                    be along lines desired by our Government.</p>
                <p>President Barclay points out that it is not made clear by what parties
                    “ratification” will be brought into effect.</p>
                <p>The Liberian Government will leave to the American Government the question of
                    compensation for use of property leased under proposed arrangement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
